Use our current algorithm for channel assignment
Determine number of channels by finding enough channels to accomodate all fragments > 1% relative area 
Fit fragments into sets of 3 channels, each set of three called a  "method", prioritizinng by % relative area
Do not repeat a peak within a method (3 channels) 
Do not include overlapping RT windows within a channel. 
Do not overlap integration, collection, or peak drift windows within a single channel. 
Fit as many of the high signal peptides (>5% relative area) into the first three channels as possible. Start with the highest percent relative area peaks and the ones protected due to their valuable sequence coverage. 
Once you organize the windows most compactly into the first 3 channels, back fill with lower signal peptides (between 1% to 5% relative area)
Then, backfill with any peptides below 1% relative area
Designate any remaining high signal peptides (<5%) as prioritized for the next method
